  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186172039,
      "id": "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8",
      "title": "Identifying Quadrants Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "31953f8d-8b35-595f-b07d-604d473cebdf",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-7xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **II.** At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **III.** At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we define $f(x,y)=-7xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/2c/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b05234e9-e857-5f59-9a7d-0d4e05528da5",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
