    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7e6508f0-b39d-5b31-a1ae-ed863192768f",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=5xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **II.** At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **III.** At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we define $f(x,y)=5xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/6e/6ef852c9c15dc6f591119906abe479949f929edb6dc26f21588b4de545d02da2.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
